    {
      "id": "1330",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1330,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "よ and ね are common sentence-ending particles that add feeling or nuance. よ adds emphasis and is used when giving new information or asserting something (e.g., 面白いですよ = 'It's interesting, I'm telling you!'). ね is used to seek agreement or confirmation (e.g., 面白いですね = 'It's interesting, isn't it?'). When combined as よね, they express both emphasis and a request for agreement.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 78,
